From 97e099c97bbe932cdf50399e46a59ce2c54471e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agent <agent@example.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:16:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Add S7: site-level tests for single-site networks

Follow-up analyses to S6 (LIONESS/BONOBO single-site networks):

* Pooled inference across units: sign count, median rho, Stouffer's
  method (z_i = atanh(rho_i)*sqrt(n_i-3), Z = sum/sqrt(k)) with a
  within-unit permutation null (default 5000 draws) and per-unit
  empirical p-values. Also fixed-effects OLS + Huber robust fit as a
  parametric bracket, with a note on leverage/Simpson's paradox.
* Circularity-free external test: skeleton strength vs the Urban
  discharge fraction (UDF) pressure proxy from the PANGAEA metadata,
  per basin, for both estimators.
* Trivial-score benchmark: raw vs partial Spearman controlling for
  number of detects, mean log-concentration, stream order and UDF.
* Biomarker test: nested F-test whether strength explains UDF beyond
  sum-TU alone.
* 4-panel figure (forest plot with permutation null envelope,
  estimator comparison, UDF panel, raw-vs-partial dumbbell) and four
  CSV tables written to outputs/s7_site_level/.

Wired into run_all.R as step S7 (off by default, needs S6 output).
---
